hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"160","\Allahumma a'idhhu min 'adhabi al-qabr.\"" Wa in qala: \""Allahummaj'alhu faratan wa dhakhiran li-walidayhi"","" wa shafi'an mujaban. Allahumma thaqqil bihi mawazinahuma wa a'zim bihi ajurahuma"","" wa alhiqhu bi-salih al-mu'minin"","" waj'alhu fi kafalat Ibrahim"","" wa qihi bi-rahmatika 'adhab al-jahim"","" wa abdilhu daran khayran min darah"","" wa ahlan khayran min ahlah. Allahumma ighfir li-aslafina"","" wa afratina"","" wa man sabiqana bil-iman.\"". \""O Allah"","" protect him from the punishment of the grave.\"" And if one says: \""O Allah"","" make him a forerunner and a treasure for his parents"","" and an intercessor whose intercession is accepted. O Allah"","" make him heavy in their scales"","" and magnify their reward through him"","" and join him with the righteous believers"","" and place him under the care of Ibrahim (Abraham)"","" and protect him by Your mercy from the punishment of Hellfire"","" and grant him a home better than his home"","" and a family better than his family. O Allah"","" forgive our predecessors"","" our children who have passed before us"","" and those who preceded us in faith.\"" — then that is good."""""
"161","Allahummaj'alhu lana faratan, wa salafan wa ajran.. O Allah, make him (the deceased) for us a forerunner, a predecessor, and a reward."
